  "articleBody": "Foreclosed bathrooms can be a great canvas for a refresh, but it's easy to stumble into some common pitfalls if you're not careful. One of the biggest mistakes we see is covering up moisture problems without actually fixing the source. That new paint might look great, but if there's a leak behind the wall, you're just delaying a much bigger, costlier issue. Another big no-no is ignoring hidden damage behind the tub or shower surrounds. Many times, what looks like a simple cosmetic fix can unveil extensive water damage or even mold once you start demolition. And finally, failing to budget for plumbing or electrical updates is a frequent misstep. Older homes, especially foreclosures, often have outdated systems that will need to be brought up to code once you start tearing things apart. To avoid these headaches, prioritize services that can clearly separate essential repairs from purely cosmetic upgrades. Always get a detailed, inspection-based quote, and make sure there's a contingency built in for unexpected plumbing, mold, or subfloor issues. If you suspect any active leaks, mold, or structural damage, that's your cue to call in a professional like HH Remodeling LLC. We've got the experience to uncover and address these hidden issues before they become major problems.",
